<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Limerick</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Limerick is a city in the south-west of Ireland, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-shannon">River Shannon</a>, and gives its name to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-limerick">County Limerick</a>. Founded as a Norse settlement in the 10th century, it became the capital of the O'Brien kings of Thomond before falling to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-normans">Anglo-Normans</a>. Its sieges of 1690 and 1691 ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-limerick">Treaty of Limerick</a>, which closed the Williamite war in Ireland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/limerick.jpg" alt="Limerick" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: mandoft from El Campello (Alicante), Spain · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Limerick_r%C3%ADo_(46531600435).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
